# SmartOps SOC — environment template.
#
# Copy to `.env` in the REPO ROOT (next to this file) and fill in. `.env` is
# gitignored; this file must never hold a real value. Nothing here is required:
# with none of it set, the CLI runs, every family reports honestly why it can't
# answer, and the process exits 0.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# `smartops-broker` loads it automatically, searching upward from the working
# directory (so running from `backend/` works too). A variable already set in
# your shell, CI, or a container WINS over this file -- a stale local .env must
# never override a deployment's real credentials. `--verbose` prints which file
# was loaded, which is the first thing to check when a value "isn't picked up".


# ── Model provider ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Resolved at startup, in this order:
#   1. SMARTOPS_LLM_PROVIDER, if set (bedrock | deepseek)
#   2. Bedrock, if AWS_BEDROCK_MODEL_ID is set
#   3. DeepSeek, if DEEPSEEK_API_KEY is set
#   4. Neither -> scripted dispatch, no model call, nothing billed
#
# Bedrock is the primary: setting a Bedrock model id is an explicit statement of
# intent, and a DeepSeek key left in this file will NOT quietly take over from
# it. To run DeepSeek while both are present, either comment out
# AWS_BEDROCK_MODEL_ID or set SMARTOPS_LLM_PROVIDER=deepseek.
#
# Activation is keyed on the model id rather than AWS_REGION on purpose:
# AWS_REGION is set in almost any AWS environment (S3, CloudWatch, ...), so
# keying on it would select Bedrock for deployments that never intended to use a
# model at all.
#
# This is configuration, not failover: a Bedrock outage does NOT fall through to
# DeepSeek mid-run. Retrying a failed call on a different provider would change
# which model and which price served a request, silently.

# SMARTOPS_LLM_PROVIDER=bedrock

# --- AWS Bedrock (primary) ---
#
# ⚠️ There is no default model id. Strands uses the legacy Converse path, whose
# inference-profile id carries a date suffix that cannot be guessed, and a
# placeholder that looks configured but 404s on the first call is worse than a
# startup error. Resolve yours:
#
#   aws bedrock list-inference-profiles --region "$AWS_REGION" \
#     --query "inferenceProfileSummaries[?contains(inferenceProfileId,'sonnet')].inferenceProfileId"
#
# The us./eu. prefix is required for on-demand throughput.
# AWS_BEDROCK_MODEL_ID=us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6-XXXXXXXX-v1:0

# Required when Bedrock is selected. Passed to Strands explicitly, and the run
# refuses to start without it: AWS_REGION loses to a configured AWS profile, and
# Strands then silently defaults to us-west-2 -- which would ship investigation
# data to the wrong region with no error and no log line.
# AWS_REGION=us-east-1

# Credentials use the standard AWS chain, so these are optional if you already
# have a profile or an instance role. Nothing in this project reads them
# directly; boto3 does.
# AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=

# Which PRICING key bills this model. Normally you do NOT need this -- it is
# inferred from the model id (…claude-sonnet-4-6… -> claude-sonnet-4-6). Set it
# only for a model whose family can't be read from its id, in which case the run
# refuses to start rather than billing against the wrong tier.
# SMARTOPS_PRICING_KEY=claude-sonnet-4-6

# --- DeepSeek (cheaper alternative) ---
# ⚠️ Selecting DeepSeek currently fails at startup: there is no PRICING entry
# for it yet, because its published per-million-token rates are still needed.
# That failure is deliberate -- a missing rate would otherwise report the
# cheapest provider as free and disable budget gating on it.
# DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=


# ── Subagent-analysts model (Foundation-Sec-8B-Reasoning, Bedrock import) ─────
#
# The three domain analysts (identity, network, endpoint) that ANALYZE the
# broker's fetched evidence run on a Bedrock CUSTOM-IMPORTED model (Cisco
# Foundation AI's Foundation-Sec-8B-Reasoning, Llama-3.1-8B). It is invoked with
# raw invoke_model (not Converse), so it is configured separately from the
# Broker's model above. Unset -> the analysis step is skipped and the run still
# ends cleanly at the broker report.
#
# The imported-model ARN (from the Bedrock console / import job), e.g.
#   arn:aws:bedrock:us-east-1:<account>:imported-model/<id>
# SMARTOPS_ANALYST_MODEL_ARN=

# Credential for the analyst model. Two accepted forms:
#   - a Bedrock API key (bearer token) beginning with "ABSK..."
#   - AWS creds as ACCESS_KEY_ID:SECRET_ACCESS_KEY[:SESSION_TOKEN]
# Optional: if unset, boto3's normal credential chain (env / profile / role) and
# AWS_REGION above are used, same as the Broker's Bedrock model.
# SMARTOPS_ANALYST_API_KEY=

# Optional generation controls.
#
# Temperature deliberately does NOT match the model's generation_config (0.6): that is
# its conversational default, and a SOC verdict is not a conversation. Measured at 0.6,
# one evidence slice produced three of the four possible dispositions across five draws
# -- confidence spread 0.60, citation Jaccard 0.27. See
# docs/sessions/handover_2026-08-27_analyst-verdict-variance.md. 0.3 is the model card's
# own evaluation setting. 0 gives byte-identical draws but thinner reads.
# SMARTOPS_ANALYST_TEMPERATURE=0.3
# SMARTOPS_ANALYST_TOP_P=0.95
# SMARTOPS_ANALYST_MAX_GEN_LEN=3072


# ── Splunk (siem family, over MCP) ────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Referenced as ${VAR} from mcp_servers.json, so no secret lives in the repo.
# Unset means the server is skipped and `siem` reports "no MCP server
# configured" -- not a crash.
# SPLUNK_MCP_URL=https://splunk.example.com:8089/services/mcp
# SPLUNK_TOKEN=

# Point at a different mcpServers config (default: ./mcp_servers.json)
# SMARTOPS_MCP_CONFIG=/etc/smartops/mcp_servers.json

# Comma-separated MCP server names whose TLS certificate is NOT verified.
# Unset (the default) verifies every server. LEAVE IT UNSET unless you have a
# specific reason -- disabling verification sends that server's bearer token to
# whatever host answers on its address, and trusts whatever comes back as SOC
# evidence.
#
# The case it exists for: a Splunk management port (8089) still using the stock
# `CN=SplunkServerDefaultCert`. That certificate is issued by `SplunkCommonCA`,
# which no public trust store carries, AND it has no subjectAltName -- so
# importing the CA still fails hostname verification against an IP, because
# Python no longer falls back to CN. Replacing the certificate with one carrying
# a proper SAN is the durable fix; this is the escape hatch until then.
# SMARTOPS_MCP_TLS_NO_VERIFY=splunk


# ── Splunk skill pack (siem family) ───────────────────────────────────────────
#
# One switch governing both halves of the pack: a routing table injected into the
# `siem` system prompt, and the `read_reference` tool appended to the `siem`
# toolset. They move together on purpose -- a run with the table but not the tool
# is a configuration nobody can name afterwards when reading the cost ledger.
#
# OFF by default, and the benchmark pins it off regardless of what is set here,
# so a measured run is always a clean one. Truthy values are 1/true/yes/on.
# Turning it on changes the siem tool count and token cost, so a run made with it
# on is not comparable to a baseline made without it.
# SMARTOPS_SKILLS_ENABLED=0


# ── VirusTotal (vt family, REST) ──────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Free tier allows ~4 requests/minute; lookups run sequentially because of it.
# Unset means `vt` reports the missing key rather than failing.
# VT_API_KEY=


# ── Observability ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Nothing is exported by default: Strands' GenAI spans can carry prompt and
# response content, and this is a SOC tool.
#
# Point at any OTLP collector (Langfuse, Phoenix, CloudWatch) to enable export.
# Langfuse is auto-detected from the endpoint and needs no code change.
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=

# ⚠️ Set this before enabling any exporter. Strands' span-content redaction is
# OPT-IN and off by default -- absent this, prompts and responses are exported
# verbatim. An empty value after the `=` means "redact everything sensitive".
# OTEL_SEMCONV_STABILITY_OPT_IN=gen_ai_unredacted_attributes=
